.TH SDL_murmur3_32 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_murmur3_32 \- Calculate a 32-bit MurmurHash3 value for a block of data.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "Uint32 SDL_murmur3_32(const void *data, size_t len, Uint32 seed);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
https://en\[char46]wikipedia\[char46]org/wiki/MurmurHash
.PP
A seed may be specified, which changes the final results consistently, but this does not work like
.BR SDL_crc16
and
.BR SDL_crc32 :
you can\(aqt feed a previous result from this function back into itself as the next seed value to calculate a hash in chunks; it won\(aqt produce the same hash as it would if the same data was provided in a single call\[char46]
.PP
If you aren\(aqt sure what to provide for a seed, zero is fine\[char46] Murmur3 is not cryptographically secure, so it shouldn\(aqt be used for hashing top-secret data\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I data
the data to be hashed\[char46]
.TP
.I len
the size of data, in bytes\[char46]
.TP
.I seed
a value that alters the final hash value\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a Murmur3 32-bit hash value\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

